cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  scijit: scipy-equivalent numerical routines callable inside
  numba @njit code
message: >-
  scijit wraps established Fortran numerical libraries so they can
  be called from inside numba @njit-compiled code. If you use it,
  please cite this package AND the upstream libraries it wraps (listed
  under references), whose authors did the underlying numerical work.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Shmuel
    family-names: Gilbaum
    affiliation: The Hebrew University of Jerusalem
    email: shmuel.gilbaum@mail.huji.ac.il
license: MIT
references:
  # --- architecture & existing numba wrappers this project builds on ---
  - type: software
    title: NumbaMinpack
    authors:
      - given-names: Nicholas
        family-names: Wogan
    url: "https://github.com/Nicholaswogan/NumbaMinpack"
    notes: >-
      Demonstrated the approach scijit is built on: calling a
      compiled Fortran pack from inside numba @njit code via a @cfunc
      address and a bind(c) wrapper. scijit keeps its low-level MINPACK
      signatures (minpack_sig, hybrd, lmdif); the public fsolve/leastsq
      follow scipy. MIT license.
  - type: software
    title: "odepack (thread-safe modern-Fortran ODEPACK)"
    authors:
      - given-names: Nicholas
        family-names: Wogan
    url: "https://github.com/Nicholaswogan/odepack"
    notes: >-
      The modern-Fortran ODEPACK edition (LSODA/LSODAR) actually
      vendored and wrapped by scijit.integrate. Underlying ODEPACK
      algorithm by A. C. Hindmarsh (LLNL).
  - type: software
    title: numbalsoda
    authors:
      - given-names: Nicholas
        family-names: Wogan
    url: "https://github.com/Nicholaswogan/numbalsoda"
    notes: >-
      scijit.integrate's lsoda_sig cfunc signature matches this
      package's; scijit's odeint itself follows scipy's API.
  # --- the numerical libraries themselves ---
  - type: software
    title: FITPACK
    authors:
      - given-names: Paul
        family-names: Dierckx
    notes: "Dierckx splines -> scijit.interpolate. Netlib, public domain."
  - type: software
    title: "MINPACK (fortran-lang modern edition)"
    authors:
      - name: fortran-lang / Argonne National Laboratory
    url: "https://github.com/fortran-lang/minpack"
    notes: "Garbow, Hillstrom & More. -> scijit.optimize. MIT + UChicago."
  - type: software
    title: L-BFGS-B
    authors:
      - given-names: Jorge
        family-names: Nocedal
      - name: "Zhu, Byrd, Morales; modern edition by Jacob Williams"
    url: "https://github.com/jacobwilliams/lbfgsb"
    notes: "-> scijit.optimize.minimize(L-BFGS-B). BSD-3."
  - type: software
    title: SLSQP
    authors:
      - given-names: Dieter
        family-names: Kraft
      - name: "modern edition by Jacob Williams"
    url: "https://github.com/jacobwilliams/slsqp"
    notes: "-> scijit.optimize (SLSQP). BSD-3."
  - type: software
    title: PRIMA
    authors:
      - given-names: Zaikun
        family-names: Zhang
      - name: "reference implementation of M. J. D. Powell's solvers"
    url: "https://github.com/libprima/prima"
    notes: "UOBYQA/NEWUOA/BOBYQA/LINCOA/COBYLA -> scijit.optimize. BSD-3."
  - type: software
    title: "QUADPACK (modern edition)"
    authors:
      - name: "Piessens, de Doncker; modern edition by Jacob Williams"
    url: "https://github.com/jacobwilliams/quadpack"
    notes: "-> scijit.integrate.quad. BSD-3."
  - type: software
    title: "LAPACK (Reference-LAPACK) + BLAS"
    authors:
      - name: "E. Anderson, Z. Bai, J. Dongarra et al. (LAPACK team)"
    url: "https://github.com/Reference-LAPACK/lapack"
    notes: >-
      Full reference LAPACK + BLAS, vendored as the shared
      scijit/_lib/liblapackref that backs scijit.optimize's
      least-squares path (curve_fit, lsq_linear). BSD-3.
